{"title":"2022 SSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A monic polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> has real roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa7e4dae453f67aa78269d730f7cae70296659a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s,t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> and a monic polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84e820e988dc3452c71b81d4e3ed189382cc1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3,s^3,t^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />. The minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828b2f9aed8bd89b3f0d4a2aec0553d3896fb811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{g(1)}{f(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"40\" height=\"45\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad3c183d420a9f5d6df8b296d0a61cf0f062204.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x):(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)\\quad\\text{and}\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803bcee09b95b8797ee7f297a097c6ee655ccf7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x):(x-r^3)(x-s^3)(x-t^3).\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" /> So, \\begin{align*} \\frac{g(1)}{f(1)}&amp;=\\frac{(1-r^3)(1-s^3)(1-r^3)}{(1-r)(1-s)(1-t)}\\\\ &amp;=(1+r+r^2)(1+s+s^2)(1+t+t^2)\\\\ &amp;=\\left(\\left(r+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\left(\\left(s+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\left(\\left(t+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\\\ &amp;\\ge\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{27}{64}\\implies 27+64=\\boxed{91}. \\end{align*}\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017140107\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 56/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1947/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26194:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017140107 and revision id 280148. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}